.TH ORANGE-AGENT 1 2026-10-18 orange "User Commands"
.SH NAME
orange-agent \- keep XMPP sessions open for orange-cli
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B orange-agent
.RI [ option ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B orange-agent
is a per-user daemon that holds the client's XMPP sessions and serves
them to
.BR orange-cli (1)
on a unix socket.
It is not implemented yet: started without options, it prints the
socket path it would use and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display a usage message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Output version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
The socket is
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/orange/agent.sock .
It must be set to an absolute path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for
.B \-\-help
and
.BR \-\-version ,
1 otherwise, 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR orange-cli (1),
.BR oranged (8)
.PP
The full documentation is the Texinfo manual:
.B info orange
